😂 A little play in the joint.

Too tightly screwed down and every representation gets treated as reality itself. Too loose and you lose contact with reality altogether.

The useful zone is:

\boxed{
\text{Reality Surfing}
=
\text{Representational Freedom}
+
\text{Reality Tether}
}

Loosen the model, not reality.

That lets you temporarily entertain “What if scale works like this?”, “What if API is an appendix?”, “What if this metaphor is executable?” without requiring any of them to be literally true.

Then surf back through Reality Stitch:

\text{depart}
\rightarrow
\text{play}
\rightarrow
\text{discover}
\rightarrow
\text{return}
\rightarrow
\text{test}

So yeah:

You need a screw loose—but preferably one with a retaining washer. ;)

Enough wobble to discover another degree of freedom. Enough attachment to bring the discovery home.